# Die for real, then look at the gravestone (bd inc-r6z).
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/gates/Options.Dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/gravestone.keys 11
#
# The seed and the settings are not free choices. tools/check_headless.sh:387
# already keeps one reproducible confirmed death -- dive.keys, seed 11, the
# pinned gate settings -- and this file replays exactly that scenario so it
# does not have to find a second one. The pinned settings run with OPT_NODEATH
# on, so the killing blow asks "You die... Die? [yn]" (src/Fight.cpp) and every
# remaining dive.keys keystroke is swallowed by that prompt until a 'y'
# arrives. The trailing y's below are that 'y'; some of them may instead be
# spent on OPT_ELUDE_DEATH's budgeted escapes, which is why there are twelve.
#
# After Player::Death() runs, src/Main.cpp:481 waits for ENTER and then calls
# Player::Gravestone(), which draws GravestoneImage (src/Main.cpp:2305) with
# ch = 'g' before it asks for anything. So the screen dumped below IS the death
# screen a player sees. 'q' is what the gravestone's own prompt
# ("[dvmqs]", src/Main.cpp:2434) accepts for Quit; @quit would not be read
# there.

@include dive.keys

y*12
ENTER*3

@dump:gravestone

q
